"""Write a current findings document from reconciled audit results."""
from pathlib import Path
import json
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
s=json.loads((R/'summary.json').read_text());a=s['all']
lines=['# Repository notebook-format coverage within the issue #5 inventory','',f"Of the fixed {a['sources']:,} source identities, {a['mapped']} have mapped GitHub repositories. All were checked at their previously recorded revisions: **{a['present']} contain detected notebook/literate-document formats**, {a['none_detected']} have none detected under this protocol, and {a['unknown']} is unknown. The {a['unmapped']} unmapped sources are outside the repository denominator.",'',f"Detected formats occur in {s['primary_domains_with_detections']} of {s['primary_domains_total']} original primary-domain labels (including infrastructure and general-purpose labels). The confirmed-detection fraction is {a['present']}/{a['mapped']} = {a['present']/a['mapped']:.1%}; this is not an estimate of notebook quality or population-wide biological coverage.",'','## Format counts','', '| Format | Repositories with detection |','| --- | ---: |']
for f,n in sorted(a['formats'].items(),key=lambda x:-x[1]):lines.append(f'| {f} | {n} |')
lines += ['', 'Counts overlap across formats. Extension matches are not content validation; the marimo/Pluto/Jupytext signature probes are incomplete. Paired documents and rendered exports can be duplicates.', '',f"The scan performed {s['signature_probes']} bounded text-prefix probes and left {s['unprobed_text_files']:,} other text files unprobed. It found {s['notebook_paths_found']:,} supported paths/signatures, not that many independent analyses.",'','## Primary domains','', '| Original primary domain | All sources | Mapped | Present | None detected | Unknown | Unmapped |', '| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
for d,v in s['domains'].items():lines.append('| '+d+' | '+' | '.join(str(v[k]) for k in ['sources','mapped','present','none_detected','unknown','unmapped'])+' |')
lines += ['','## Original ranking routes','','Each route has 300 identities; membership overlaps between routes.','','| Route | Mapped | Present | None detected | Unknown | Unmapped |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
for d,v in s['routes'].items():lines.append('| '+d+' | '+' | '.join(str(v[k]) for k in ['mapped','present','none_detected','unknown','unmapped'])+' |')
lines += ['','## Interpretation','','This answers which parts of the previously selected software inventory have detectable notebook or literate-document files. It avoids choosing a few notebooks to create apparent breadth, but inherits the inventory selection and its assistant-assigned labels. Repository labels are not notebook-content labels. The supported formats include prose-oriented literate documents, so the positive set is a pool for further inspection, not a set of validated biological workflows.','','None detected is not exhaustive absence: arbitrary text-notebook filenames, external links, other branches and submodules can be missed. Unknown tree responses remain explicit. Source revisions were fixed by the earlier study, while tree/prefix retrievals are new observations. No biological analyses were run.','','See [protocol](README.md), [input provenance](input-provenance.json), [observations](observations.jsonl), [group CSV](domain-coverage.csv), [format CSV](domain-formats.csv) and [validation](validation.json).']
(R/'results.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
